<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Judicial Committee of the Privy Council</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1833">1833</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Judicial Committee of the Privy Council, set up in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1833, served as the final court of appeal for British colonies and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">dominions</a>. Its rulings settled many imperial disputes, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sobhuza-ii">Sobhuza II</a>'s unsuccessful land case from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eswatini">Swaziland</a> in 1926 and the 1927 award that gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> the interior of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/labrador">Labrador</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>'s claim.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/judicial-committee-of-the-privy-council.jpg" alt="Judicial Committee of the Privy Council" width="320" height="564" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Arms_of_the_United_Kingdom_(Privy_Council)_Tudor_Crown_and_Gaelic_Harp.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
